    "previous_model_response": "Since \\(OA\\) is a radius to the point of tangency, it is perpendicular to the tangent line at \\(A\\). Thus,\n\n\\[\nx+80^\\circ=90^\\circ\n\\]\n\nso\n\n\\[\nx=10^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nAlso, \\(OA=OB\\) because they are radii, so \\(\\triangle OAB\\) is isosceles. Therefore,\n\n\\[\nz=x=10^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nAnswer: E. 10",
    "correction": "Source GT A/80? corrected to E/10?."
  },
